panasonic-fz-g1 (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Auto-rotate while undocked: an [autorotate] profile for convertible-helper
    1.3.0 (GNOME does not rotate this tablet by itself).

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0700

panasonic-fz-g1 (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depend on panasonic-hbtn-dkms 1.4.0, which reports the bezel buttons A1
    and A2 as XF86Launch1 and XF86Launch2 keys; bind them in GNOME's Settings,
    Keyboard, Custom Shortcuts.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0700

panasonic-fz-g1 (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: unblock the panasonic_laptop module and re-write the
    Panasonic brightness register once at boot, so GNOME's brightness control
    works on the Panasonic Toughpad FZ-G1 (Mk1, Debian 13, kernel 6.12).
  * Profile for convertible-helper: detaching the keyboard dock (USB 2047:0318
    disappears) counts as tablet mode.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:30:00 -0700
